# {{packageName}} Agent Guide

This hook follows the richer ReDBox client hook archetype generated by `@researchdatabox/redbox-dev-tools init`.

Keep these rules in place unless the user explicitly asks to change the hook model.

## Project Shape

- `src/index.ts` is the hook entry point and compiles to `dist/index.js`.
- `src/config/` contains config returned from `registerRedboxConfig()`.
- `src/form-config/` contains typed form definitions returned from `registerRedboxFormConfigs()`.
- `src/migrations/` contains the synchronous hook migration registry.
- `support/bootstrap-data/`, `assets/`, `views/`, and `language-defaults/` hold client material used by the Docker harness and hook runtime.
- `support/development/` and `support/integration-testing/` contain the local portal and Mocha harnesses.

## Dependency Contract

- `@researchdatabox/redbox-core` is the runtime compatibility anchor.
- `@researchdatabox/redbox-dev-tools` is the shared authoring and test toolchain.
- Direct hook `dependencies` are reserved for hook-owned runtime packages only.

Do not directly add shared runtime or toolchain packages such as:

- `axios`
- `rxjs`
- `lodash`
- `typescript`
- `ts-node`
- `mocha`
- `chai`
- `@researchdatabox/sails-ng-common`

## Compile And Test

Use the existing scripts in `package.json`.

Do not replace the custom `run-hook-tsc` or `run-hook-mocha` entrypoints with plain `tsc` or `mocha`.

## Config And Migrations

Prefer returning config from `registerRedboxConfig()` instead of mutating `sails.config` in `configure()`.

Keep `registerRedboxMigrations()` synchronous. Add new migration modules to `src/migrations/index.ts`, and give each migration a unique hook-prefixed, sortable name such as `{{packageName}}:20260703T000000-seed-client-defaults`.

## Docker Runtime

The docker compose files intentionally set `NODE_PATH` so a mounted hook can resolve host-provided runtime dependencies from the Redbox portal dependency tree.

Do not remove that unless the runtime install model changes deliberately.

For mounted-core development, update `support/development/core-mount.env` or pass `REDBOX_PORTAL_PATH` in the environment, then use `npm run dev:run:core`. Do not hand-edit the generated `support/development/.tmp/core-mount.env` file.
